.TH "MAKNOON" "1" "Jan 2024" "Maknoon Post-Quantum Engine" "Maknoon Manual"

.SH NAME
maknoon-call - Invoke an MCP tool on a running Maknoon agent via a standard SSE client


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon call [tool_name] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes an MCP tool using a standard SSE client.
By default, this command uses HTTPS with Post-Quantum TLS 1.3 (ML-KEM)
to ensure a quantum-resistant orchestration handshake.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--addr\fP="localhost:8080"
	Address of the running Maknoon agent

.PP
\fB--args\fP=""
	JSON string of tool arguments

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for call

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Skip TLS certificate verification (ONLY FOR TESTING)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB--passphrase-fd\fP=0
	Read passphrase from file descriptor N (e.g., --passphrase-fd 3  3<<<$(pass show key)). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FD

.PP
\fB--passphrase-file\fP=""
	Read passphrase from a file instead of prompting (use - for stdin). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FILE

.PP
\fB--policy\fP=""
	Path to a declarative governance policy file (JSON)

.PP
\fB--tpm\fP[=false]
	Enable TPM 2.0 hardware-backed storage for keys

.PP
\fB--tpm-device\fP="/dev/tpmrm0"
	Path to the TPM device node

.PP
\fB--tpm-pcrs\fP=[]
	List of PCRs to bind keys to (e.g., 7,14)

.PP
\fB--trace\fP[=false]
	Enable low-level diagnostic tracing to stderr


